WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.760
Many developing neurons survive because a neurotrophin activates the right Trk

2
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.300
receptor, said "track".

3
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:16.040
These receptors are kinases that switch on signals supporting survival and growth.

4
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.940
That is how a neuron reads the factor its target supplies.

5
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:25.100
The match matters: different groups of neurons depend on different factors and

6
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.300
receptors. How does that survival signal start?

7
00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:31.293
Mammals make four neurotrophins.

8
00:00:32.193 --> 00:00:37.193
NGF prefers TrkA. BDNF and NT-4 prefer TrkB.

9
00:00:37.993 --> 00:00:42.613
NT-3 prefers TrkC, and activates TrkA and TrkB more weakly.

10
00:00:43.533 --> 00:00:45.993
Each factor is a dimer of two identical chains.

11
00:00:46.893 --> 00:00:49.013
It brings two Trk receptors together.

12
00:00:49.973 --> 00:00:52.173
Their kinase domains phosphorylate each other.

13
00:00:52.973 --> 00:00:59.113
The phosphorylated tyrosines start survival signals through Ras to ERK and PI3K to

14
00:00:59.113 --> 00:01:00.113
Akt.

15
00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:03.393
Targets make a limited amount of survival factor.

16
00:01:04.393 --> 00:01:05.973
Neurons that fail to get enough die.

17
00:01:06.813 --> 00:01:11.953
Which factor a population depends on tracks the Trk receptor it makes and the factor

18
00:01:11.953 --> 00:01:17.093
its target makes. So the receptor map helps explain which developing neurons

19
00:01:17.093 --> 00:01:18.093
survive.

20
00:01:18.617 --> 00:01:20.717
Mouse knockouts test those dependencies.

21
00:01:21.777 --> 00:01:27.397
Without NGF or TrkA, mice lose sympathetic neurons and many small sensory neurons

22
00:01:27.397 --> 00:01:28.437
for pain and heat.

23
00:01:29.297 --> 00:01:32.537
Without BDNF, they lose sensory neurons for balance.

24
00:01:33.417 --> 00:01:38.297
Without NT-3 or TrkC, they lose sensory neurons that report limb position.

25
00:01:39.277 --> 00:01:41.437
Different pairs give different patterns of loss.

26
00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:46.567
A shared receptor, p75, binds all four neurotrophins.

27
00:01:47.427 --> 00:01:52.847
It has no kinase. It belongs to the tumor necrosis factor receptor family and

28
00:01:52.847 --> 00:01:54.047
carries a death domain.

29
00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:56.767
But its response depends on its partners.

30
00:01:57.687 --> 00:02:00.087
With TrkA, it can raise NGF binding.

31
00:02:00.087 --> 00:02:03.187
With sortilin, it can carry a death signal.

32
00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:06.987
Precursor processing adds another variable.

33
00:02:07.967 --> 00:02:10.747
NGF starts as a longer chain, proNGF.

34
00:02:11.627 --> 00:02:12.847
Cells can secrete it uncut.

35
00:02:13.647 --> 00:02:20.487
In Hempstead's experiments, uncut proNGF bound p75 tightly and triggered apoptosis

36
00:02:20.487 --> 00:02:22.287
of cultured sympathetic neurons.

37
00:02:23.227 --> 00:02:25.427
Later work showed that this death needs sortilin.

38
00:02:26.347 --> 00:02:29.007
Mature NGF supported survival through TrkA.

39
00:02:29.887 --> 00:02:34.787
Another group found that uncut proNGF could support survival too, more weakly.

40
00:02:35.707 --> 00:02:38.847
The outcome depends on processing and the balance of receptors.
